oft.Network/virtualNetworks/join/action</code> permission on the virtual ne=
twork. Assigning these roles at the specific resource scopes satisfies the =
requirement and adheres to the principle of least privilege.<br></p><p><cod=
e><strong>Private DNS Zone Contributor only</strong></code> is <strong>inco=
rrect</strong> because although this role allows management of private DNS =
zones and creation of virtual network links, it does not grant sufficient p=
ermissions on the target virtual network resource. Without the <code>virtua=
lNetworks/join/action</code> permission at the VNet scope, the link operati=
on fails.<br></p><p><code><strong>Network Contributor only</strong></code> =
is <strong>incorrect</strong> because it grants permissions on virtual netw=
ork resources but does not include rights to manage private DNS zones or cr=
eate DNS virtual network links. Therefore, it cannot be used to link the DN=
S zone to the virtual network.<br></p><p><code><strong>Contributor only</st=
rong></code> is <strong>incorrect</strong> because it provides full access =
to all resource types at the assigned scope, which exceeds the permissions =
required for this task and violates the principle of least privilege.</p><p=
